{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>When it set out</b> — 2. העלות הענן (when the cloud set out) — העלות הגולה (when the exile set out): this is what they said: they were worthy that a נם should be made for them in the days of Ezra, in the manner that was made for them in the days of Moses, but sin caused [it not to happen]." "<b>And at the place</b> — 2 in the Masorah: here and the other: ובמקום גדולים אל תעמוד (and at the place of great ones do not stand) — that they would not relieve themselves neither in front of it nor to its sides but behind it. This is ובמקום אשר ישכון שם הענן (and at the place where the cloud dwells there) — i.e., in front of it or to its sides, do not stand to make גדולים there."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The word נם appears to be an abbreviation or possibly corrupt; translated hyper-literally as written. The phrase 'this is what they said' introduces a rabbinic statement, but no further attribution is given.", 1 "The Masorah citation 'ובמקום גדולים אל תעמוד' is likely an allusive phrase built from two verse-occurrences of ובמקום; the word גדולים (great ones) functions both as part of the allusive reading and as a euphemism for bodily relief, as the comment explains."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:46.394045031Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}